      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The parallelogram generated by $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$ is formed by taking the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$, where $\\overrightarrow{AB} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}.$\nThe area of the parallelogram is given by the magnitude of the cross product of these two vectors.\n\\begin{align*}\n\\overrightarrow{AB} \\times \\overrightarrow{AC} &= \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{vmatrix} -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\end{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} - \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 \\end{vmatrix} \\mathbf{j} + \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n&= (-6 - 4) \\mathbf{i} - (-2 - 12) \\mathbf{j} + (1 + 9) \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n&= \\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 10 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\end{align*} Taking the magnitude of this vector, we find that $\\|\\overrightarrow{AB} \\times \\overrightarrow{AC}\\| = \\sqrt{(-10)^2 + 14^2 + 10^2} = \\sqrt{100 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{396} = 6\\sqrt{11}.$\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram is $\\boxed{6\\sqrt{11}}.$\nThe answer is: 6\\sqrt{11}",
