      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to compute the magnitude of their cross product. The area of the parallelogram is given by the absolute value of the scalar triple product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{a})\\).\n\nFirst, we compute the cross product \\(\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{a}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{a} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\end{vmatrix}\n= \\mathbf{i}((-3)(-2) - (4)(1)) - \\mathbf{j}((1)(-2) - (4)(3)) + \\mathbf{k}((1)(1) - (-3)(3))\n= \\mathbf{i}(6 - 4) - \\mathbf{j}(-2 - 12) + \\mathbf{k}(1 + 9)\n= 2\\mathbf{i} + 14\\mathbf{j} + 10\\mathbf{k}\n= \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of the cross product:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{a}\\| = \\sqrt{2^2 + 14^2 + 10^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{300} = 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]",
